    "updated_at": "2019-09-05T18:02:40Z",
    "body": "1. The text is self-contradictory, but I think it cannot be fixed in a meaningful way without changing the results. Neither should it. Instead the algorithm should be fixed to follow the intended result, which should remain: \"This snaps the start of the selection to the start of the new text if it was in the middle of the text that it replaced\"\r\n\r\n2. Yes. I filed identical bugs here: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1578395 and here: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1000275",
