    "updated_at": "2019-09-06T06:50:23Z",
    "body": "Going back one sentence:\r\n\r\n> 3. If selection start is greater than end, then increment it by delta. (If delta is negative, i.e. the new text is shorter than the old text, then this will decrease the value of selection start.)\r\n\r\nI think it is a off-by-one error in this sentence, it should read: \"If selection start is greater than _**or equal to**_ end, then increment it by delta.\"\r\n\r\nThis makes sense now (in the 3rd input): https://jsfiddle.net/thenlich/s24xcwk6/",
