    "created_at": "2019-09-07T05:57:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-07T05:57:32Z",
    "body": "To answer https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4886#issuecomment-528540346 the current result of the algorithm in clause 3 can be described as:\r\n\r\n> This snaps the start of the selection to the start of the new text if it was in the middle of **_or adjacent to_** the text that it replaced.\r\n\r\nWhile the equivalent statement in clause 4 remains:\r\n\r\n> This snaps the end of the selection to the end of the new text if it was in the middle of the text that it replaced.\r\n\r\nI can not imagine that this asymmetry between start and end of selection was intended when \"preserve\" was added to the spec.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
